# cuts/v1.0.26/cut.env -- the pins bin/rollforward_gate.sh binds for --cut v1.0.26
#
# The gate reads exactly TWO keys, and the mapping is DECLARED in the runner:
#     OSTLER_PIN_OA="$(_cut_pin DAEMON_COMMIT)"
#     OSTLER_PIN_CM051="$(_cut_pin CM051)"
# Everything else is prose the gate never touches. Keep it that way: the v1.0.24
# attempt to vendor OS003's fuller records dragged 464 lines of operator working
# notes, four private box IPs and five notarisation IDs into the product repo.
#
# WHY v1.0.26 EXISTS. NOTHING HAS BEEN CUT SINCE 2026-08-08. Eight tagged runs
# produced no DMG -- v1.0.23 once, v1.0.24 four times, v1.0.25 three times --
# every one dying at check-ostler-app because OSTLER_APP_PATH defaults to a
# sibling ostler-assistant checkout that cannot exist on a hosted runner, and
# nothing in the pipeline fetched the bundle. Ostler.app was built locally and
# published nowhere, so `ship` demanded an artefact with no published home.
#
# v1.0.25's own header says it was "the first that can exercise the wire". It
# could not: #612 gave CI a token for the DAEMON, and the Hub app was a separate
# artefact in a separate repo that no credential covered and no step fetched.
# Fixing the daemon fetch simply moved the failure one gate later.
#
# #624 adds download-hub-app: fetch the published tarball, verify SHA-256
# fail-closed exactly as download-daemon does, extract AT OSTLER_APP_PATH, and
# no-op when a locally built bundle is already there. The gate is UNCHANGED --
# a missing Hub app used to be non-fatal and shipped a silently Hub-less DMG
# (v1018-D668), so failing closed is correct and stays.

# The daemon this DMG ships. UNCHANGED from v1.0.25: gui/Makefile still carries
# DAEMON_VERSION ?= 0.4.55, and this cut alters no daemon pin.
#
# hub-v0.4.55 is an ANNOTATED tag: the ref points at tag object d40c3535 and the
# COMMIT is e0234e71. Pinning the tag object would name a non-commit and every
# ancestry check would fail in a way that reads as a stale daemon rather than a
# malformed pin.
DAEMON_COMMIT=e0234e71c66d

# CM051 main at tag time -- 1b4ce18d, the merge of #626 (manifest + version stamp).
#
# The gate reads install.sh AT THIS REF:
#     repos/<CM051_REPO>/contents/install.sh?ref=$CM051_REF
# so the pin must name a tree whose install.sh is the one in the DMG. Every
# commit in this cut (#624 gui/Makefile + tests + workflow, #625 cut-deferrals,
# #626 manifest + version stamps, and this file) leaves install.sh untouched, so
# the pin stays truthful as those land. Re-point this key whenever a merge lands
# in a file a gate reads -- that is the v1.0.25 lesson, where leaving the pin
# behind #618 would have gated an install.sh nobody was cutting.
#
# It is at or after edff9c9e (#612, cross-org daemon token) and carries the
# 1.0.25 -> 1.0.26 version bump across all 5 stamp sites with 0 residual, so
# installer version-consistency holds.
CM051=1b4ce18d
